-- title:
--   Splitting a primitive modulo [q] into j₀- and Frobenius-typed parts
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and $j_0 : \mathbb{Z}_{q^2} \to k$ a ring homomorphism from the Witt vectors of the field with $q^2$ elements. Let $X_0$ be a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $k$ with respect to $j_0$: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F = X_0.F$ together with an action $a \mapsto X_0.\mathrm{act}\,a$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ by endomorphism tuples and a uniformiser series, satisfying the speciality condition on the Lie algebra decomposition and having height $4$. Write $[q]$ for the pair of series `X₀.F.nthSeries q`, obtained by $q$-fold iteration of $F$, let $I \subseteq k[[X_1,X_2]]$ be the ideal generated by its two components, and let $J$ be the ideal of $k[[X_1,X_2,Y_1,Y_2]]$ generated by the components of $[q](X)$ and of $[q](Y)$. Let $h$ be a power series in two variables with zero constant term whose additive coboundary $h(F(X,Y)) - h(X) - h(Y)$ lies in $J$. Then there are power series $h_0, h_1$ in two variables, both with zero constant term, whose additive coboundaries lie in $J$, such that $h - (h_0 + h_1) \in I$ and such that for every $a \in \mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ one has $h_0 \circ X_0.\mathrm{act}\,a - j_0(a)\,h_0 \in I$ and $h_1 \circ X_0.\mathrm{act}\,a - j_0(\mathrm{Frobenius}\,a)\,h_1 \in I$.
--
--   This is the type-decomposition step for the space of primitives modulo $[q]$ attached to a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module: every such primitive splits, modulo the ideal generated by the $q$-series, into an eigenvector of type $j_0$ and one of type $j_0 \circ \sigma$. It is used in the proof of [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_primitives_mod_nthSeries_typed_lines_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_primitives_mod_nthSeries_typed_lines_of_finrank_eq_two), which extracts the two typed lines of primitives in the analysis of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalODModule_exists_add_typed_of_primitive_mod_nthSeries.lean

